+// Captions at once: a first guess at the language a tab will speak, from its
+// title's script, before any speech is heard. Devanagari is "hi", Bengali
+// "bn", Tamil "ta"; the script with the most characters wins, with at least
+// 3 of them; anything else (Latin titles included) gives no hint. The
+// detector corrects a wrong hint as soon as it hears speech.
+std::optional<std::string> ScriptHint(std::u16string_view title);
